LC 36 — Valid Sudoku
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Check that every row, column, and 3×3 box has no duplicate number.

Algorithm:
For each cell:
    check row
    check column
    check 3×3 box

If duplicate → false
Otherwise → true

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    bool isValidSudoku(vector<vector<char>>& b) {
        unordered_set<string> s;

        for (int i = 0; i < 9; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < 9; j++) {
                if (b[i][j] == '.') continue;

                string r = "r" + to_string(i) + b[i][j];
                string c = "c" + to_string(j) + b[i][j];
                string box = "b" + to_string(i/3*3+j/3) + b[i][j];

                if (!s.insert(r).second ||
                    !s.insert(c).second ||
                    !s.insert(box).second)
                    return false;
            }

        return true;
    }
};

EX:
Row = [5,3,.,.,7,.,.,.,.]

5 → first time ✅
3 → first time ✅
7 → first time ✅

No duplicate → valid ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(1) — only 81 cells
Space: O(1)

